      "branchId": "notes-hadith-hadith-from-your-notes-1",
      "title": "Seek refuge with Allah",
      "intro": "Narrated Abu Huraira: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, \"Satan comes to one of you and says, 'Who created so-and-so?",
      "explanationContent": "Narrated Abu Huraira: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, \"Satan comes to one of you and says, 'Who created so-and-so? 'till he says, 'Who has created your Lord?' So, when he inspires such a question, one should seek refuge with Allah and give up such thoughts.\"",
      "learnLine": "When Shaytan puts a bad question in your mind, seek Allah's protection.",
      "quote": {
        "text": "So, when he inspires such a question, one should seek refuge with Allah and give up such thoughts.",
        "reference": "Sahih al-Bukhari 3276"
      },
